What it does: Stores arbitrary text strings. It is primarily used for domain ownership verification and email anti-spoofing protocols (SPF, DKIM, DMARC).

The Analogy: An official notary stamp on your business letterhead proving that letters genuinely originated from your office and not an imposter.

sneakerhub.com Setup:

A. SPF (Sender Policy Framework): Declares that only Google Workspace servers are permitted to send emails from @sneakerhub.com:

Plaintext
sneakerhub.com.    3600    IN    TXT    "v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all"
B. Site Verification: Proving you own the domain to Google Search Console:

Plaintext
sneakerhub.com.    3600    IN    TXT    "google-site-verification=4kZ9mP7xQ8y2w"
